{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"grep -n -i 'advance.*conf\\\\|conf.*advance\\\\|appl.*before.*advance\\\\|advance.*before.*appl\\\\|asynchron' ../agent-source/rawnode_test.go ../agent-source/node_test.go ../agent-source/doc.go ../agent-source/README.md; sed -n '432,457p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '535,585p' ../agent-source/node.go; sed -n '975,1020p' ../agent-source/raft.go; sed -n '323,347p' ../agent-source/log.go; sed -n '260,291p' ../agent-source/rawnode_test.go\"","aggregated_output":"../agent-source/doc.go:172:# Usage with Asynchronous Storage Writes\n../agent-source/doc.go:177:AsynchronousStorageWrites, and can be enabled using the flag on the Config\n../agent-source/doc.go:180:When Asynchronous Storage Writes is enabled, the responsibility of code using\n../agent-source/doc.go:200:With Asynchronous Storage Writes enabled, the total state machine handling loop\n../agent-source/doc.go:223:Usage of Asynchronous Storage Writes will typically also contain a pair of\n../agent-source/doc.go:392:\tAsynchronousStorageWrites.\n../agent-source/doc.go:397:\tAsynchronousStorageWrites.\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tselect {\n\t\t\tcase n.confstatec <- cs:\n\t\t\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\t\t}\n\t\tcase <-n.tickc:\n\t\t\tn.rn.Tick()\n\t\tcase readyc <- rd:\n\t\t\tn.rn.acceptReady(rd)\n\t\t\tif !n.rn.asyncStorageWrites {\n\t\t\t\tadvancec = n.advancec\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\trd = Ready{}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treadyc = nil\n\t\tcase <-advancec:\n\t\t\tn.rn.Advance(rd)\n\t\t\trd = Ready{}\n\t\t\tadvancec = nil\n\t\tcase c := <-n.status:\n\t\t\tc <- getStatus(r)\n\t\tcase <-n.stop:\n\t\t\tclose(n.done)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn ctx.Err()\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\treturn ErrStopped\n\t}\n\tselect {\n\tcase err := <-pm.result:\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n\t\treturn ctx.Err()\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\treturn ErrStopped\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (n *node) Ready() <-chan Ready { return n.readyc }\n\nfunc (n *node) Advance() {\n\tselect {\n\tcase n.advancec <- struct{}{}:\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (n *node) ApplyConfChange(cc pb.ConfChangeI) *pb.ConfState {\n\tvar cs pb.ConfState\n\tselect {\n\tcase n.confc <- cc.AsV2():\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t}\n\tselect {\n\tcase cs = <-n.confstatec:\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t}\n\treturn &cs\n}\n\nfunc (n *node) Status() Status {\n\tc := make(chan Status)\n\tselect {\n\tcase n.status <- c:\n\t\treturn <-c\n\tcase <-n.done:\n\t\treturn Status{}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (n *node) ReportUnreachable(id uint64) {\n\tselect {\n\t\tr.logger.Debugf(\"%x ignoring MsgHup because already leader\", r.id)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif !r.promotable() {\n\t\tr.logger.Warningf(\"%x is unpromotable and can not campaign\", r.id)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif r.hasUnappliedConfChanges() {\n\t\tr.logger.Warningf(\"%x cannot campaign at term %d since there are still pending configuration changes to apply\", r.id, r.Term)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x is starting a new election at term %d\", r.id, r.Term)\n\tr.campaign(t)\n}\n\n// errBreak is a sentinel error used to break a callback-based loop.\nvar errBreak = errors.New(\"break\")\n\nfunc (r *raft) hasUnappliedConfChanges() bool {\n\tif r.raftLog.applied >= r.raftLog.committed { // in fact applied == committed\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfound := false\n\t// Scan all unapplied committed entries to find a config change. Paginate the\n\t// scan, to avoid a potentially unlimited memory spike.\n\tlo, hi := r.raftLog.applied+1, r.raftLog.committed+1\n\t// Reuse the maxApplyingEntsSize limit because it is used for similar purposes\n\t// (limiting the read of unapplied committed entries) when raft sends entries\n\t// via the Ready struct for application.\n\t// TODO(pavelkalinnikov): find a way to budget memory/bandwidth for this scan\n\t// outside the raft package.\n\tpageSize := r.raftLog.maxApplyingEntsSize\n\tif err := r.raftLog.scan(lo, hi, pageSize, func(ents []pb.Entry) error {\n\t\tfor i := range ents {\n\t\t\tif ents[i].Type == pb.EntryConfChange || ents[i].Type == pb.EntryConfChangeV2 {\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\treturn errBreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}); err != nil && err != errBreak {\n\t\tr.logger.Panicf(\"error scanning unapplied entries [%d, %d): %v\", lo, hi, err)\n\t}\n\treturn found\n\t\tif l.lastIndex() < tocommit {\n\t\t\tl.logger.Panicf(\"tocommit(%d) is out of range [lastIndex(%d)]. Was the raft log corrupted, truncated, or lost?\", tocommit, l.lastIndex())\n\t\t}\n\t\tl.committed = tocommit\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (l *raftLog) appliedTo(i uint64, size entryEncodingSize) {\n\tif l.committed < i || i < l.applied {\n\t\tl.logger.Panicf(\"applied(%d) is out of range [prevApplied(%d), committed(%d)]\", i, l.applied, l.committed)\n\t}\n\tl.applied = i\n\tl.applying = max(l.applying, i)\n\tif l.applyingEntsSize > size {\n\t\tl.applyingEntsSize -= size\n\t} else {\n\t\t// Defense against underflow.\n\t\tl.applyingEntsSize = 0\n\t}\n\tl.applyingEntsPaused = l.applyingEntsSize >= l.maxApplyingEntsSize\n}\n\nfunc (l *raftLog) acceptApplying(i uint64, size entryEncodingSize, allowUnstable bool) {\n\tif l.committed < i {\n\t\tl.logger.Panicf(\"applying(%d) is out of range [prevApplying(%d), committed(%d)]\", i, l.applying, l.committed)\n\t\t\t\t\t\tccdata, err = ccv1.Marshal()\n\t\t\t\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\t\t\t\t\t\trawNode.ProposeConfChange(ccv1)\n\t\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tccv2 := tc.cc.AsV2()\n\t\t\t\t\t\tccdata, err = ccv2.Marshal()\n\t\t\t\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\t\t\t\t\t\trawNode.ProposeConfChange(ccv2)\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tproposed = true\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Check that the last index is exactly the conf change we put in,\n\t\t\t// down to the bits. Note that this comes from the Storage, which\n\t\t\t// will not reflect any unstable entries that we'll only be presented\n\t\t\t// with in the next Ready.\n\t\t\tlastIndex, err = s.LastIndex()\n\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\n\t\t\tentries, err := s.Entries(lastIndex-1, lastIndex+1, noLimit)\n\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\t\t\trequire.Len(t, entries, 2)\n\t\t\tassert.Equal(t, []byte(\"somedata\"), entries[0].Data)\n\n\t\t\ttyp := pb.EntryConfChange\n\t\t\tif _, ok := tc.cc.AsV1(); !ok {\n\t\t\t\ttyp = pb.EntryConfChangeV2\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trequire.Equal(t, typ, entries[1].Type)\n\t\t\tassert.Equal(t, ccdata, entries[1].Data)\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > update_map.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']));m['version']=r['audit_spec_version']\nchanges={}\npreserve='The tested failed-transfer obligation and its dependencies/observation scope remain unchanged: its driver applied the actual entering configuration before Advance and the accepted assessment concerns a later healthy idle suffix. Early-Advance legality is separate and does not challenge that history.'\ndef ch(k,ss,why):changes[k]=dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=ss,rationale=why,preserves=preserve)\nb={x['id']:x for x in m['behaviors']}\nb['B-auto-leave']['unknowns']=[]\nb['B-auto-leave']['important_branches'].append('A rejected transfer-time attempt has no independent retry queue. Transfer abort clears the proposal blocker, but an otherwise idle heartbeat-only Ready/Advance suffix creates no new appliedTo invocation. A later acknowledged entry, including a new leader no-op or unrelated client work, can supply the missing retry trigger.')\nch('B-auto-leave',['M-auto','M-transfer-abort','M-apply-response','M-advance'],'Replace the answered continuation unknown with its precise conditional producer/consumer relationship; actual measured cycle and rescue remain in Candidate/check/review feedback.')\nb['B-authority']['implementation_guards'][0]='Campaign requires local voter progress, no in-progress snapshot and no configuration entry in the interval (raftLog.applied, raftLog.committed]. This is a check of recorded application accounting, not an independent callback confirming ApplyConfChange completed.'\nch('B-authority',['M-election','M-log-pointers','M-api'],'Clarify the producer of the campaign guard input under the separately documented early-Advance allowance; preserve source-level guard and the tested apply-before-Advance history.')\nb['B-application']['unknowns']=['The Node interface permits Advance while commands are still applying, whereas RawNode.Advance describes completed application. Whether early Advance may precede ApplyConfChange, rather than only the remaining business/snapshot application, is an unresolved caller-contract boundary. Node.run has separate advancec and confc handling and no additional ordering enforcement.']\nch('B-application',['M-api','M-advance','M-node-loop','M-node-advance-apply'],'Retain specific interface-ordering ambiguity discovered by following public Node calls into the common RawNode completion path; do not treat early configuration acknowledgment as established legal input.')\nfor x in m['surfaces']:\n if x['entry_point']=='raft.appliedTo -> transfer rejection -> tickHeartbeat abort':\n  x['reason']='Mapped conditional retry relationship: failed-transfer idle continuation was checked and reviewed; later application is a rescue trigger. See Candidate c1ba7e9ff9034a728850b297376ecbb8 and CheckRun e30e751a96ef45c8b43640539253ffe4 for the scoped outcome.'\n  ch('surface:'+x['entry_point'],['M-auto','M-election','M-apply-response','M-advance','M-transfer-abort'],'Replace the answered source question with scoped navigation, without claiming resolution of all AutoLeave histories.')\n if x['entry_point']=='Node.Advance before finishing application / ApplyConfChange':\n  x['reason']='Node.Advance permits overlap with ongoing application and Node.run handles advancec independently from confc. RawNode.Advance nevertheless records applied progress; hup then scans only beyond that recorded index. Determine whether the early-Advance permission includes delaying ApplyConfChange itself. If so, both automatic-exit scheduling and campaign membership freshness need new legal-history analysis; the completed failed-transfer witness does not use this ordering.'\n  x['source_ids']=['M-api','M-advance','M-node-loop','M-node-advance-apply','M-election','M-auto','M-config']\n  ch('surface:'+x['entry_point'],x['source_ids'],'Sharpen the early-Advance surface with actual producer and consumer paths while preserving unresolved normative applicability.')\nc=m['core_overview']\nc['open_details']=[x for x in c['open_details'] if not x.startswith('Whether automatic leave')]\nc['open_details'].append('The early-Advance permission must be reconciled with ApplyConfChange ordering before using delayed membership application as a legal campaign or automatic-exit history.')\nc['connection']['explanation']=c['connection']['explanation'].replace('while campaign blocks unapplied committed membership','while campaign scans for membership entries beyond the recorded applied index')\nc['connection']['explanation'] += ' Automatic exit is retried on later acknowledged application; transfer timeout itself only clears the blocker, so it does not supply this trigger in a caught-up idle cluster.'\nch('core_overview',['M-auto','M-advance','M-apply-response','M-transfer-abort','M-election','M-api'],'Remove answered continuation unknown and qualify the summary of the campaign guard by its actual accounting input; keep broader ordering question open.')\njson.dump(m,open('map_followup.json','w'),indent=2)\nsource=dict(id='M-node-advance-apply',file='node.go',start_line=550,end_line=573,kind='code_observation')\nsub=dict(action='research',rationale='Update the initial map at the natural handoff after an accepted reviewed finding, and retain substantive source-only progress on a different caller-ordering premise without inventing its legality.',map_path='map_followup.json',map_changes=changes,sources=[source],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['c1ba7e9ff9034a728850b297376ecbb8','C-auto-leave-continuation','44ecdde6ffdd41aab4fbf9cfe88f0cb8','e30e751a96ef45c8b43640539253ffe4','da3e13326803455b832beeadae1b7775','B-auto-leave','B-application','B-authority','M-node-advance-apply','M-api','M-election','M-advance'],answered='The current assessment confirms the fixed failed-transfer cycle as violated with checker correspondence reviewed and no open issues. Its conditional mechanism is now recorded in Behavior rather than left as an obsolete unknown. New source tracing of the separate early-Advance surface shows that Node.Advance and ApplyConfChange use independent channels, advance executes RawNode.Advance, and that method applies the stored completion response regardless of whether confc was processed. hasUnappliedConfChanges then scans only beyond recorded raftLog.applied. This identifies an actual timing dependency, but the public Node early-application allowance and RawNode completed-application wording do not yet resolve whether delaying ApplyConfChange across Advance is legal.',remaining=['Resolve the exact early-Advance/ApplyConfChange contract before extending the existing requirement scope or constructing another applicable check.','Under apply-before-Advance, investigate whether configuration-triggered maybeCommit can establish the first current-term commitment despite hup scanning unapplied committed configuration; no defect is presumed from missing read-release call alone.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Accepted finding remains limited to its actual completed history. New contract ambiguity is preserved as a Surface and Behavior unknown, not promoted to a finding or used to weaken caller duties.'))\njson.dump(sub,open('submission_map_followup.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 update_map.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission_map_followup.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);x=json.loads(p.stdout);print('valid',x.get('valid'));print([(d['code'],d['message']) for d in x.get('diagnostics',[])])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
